


   =====( FreeSpace V1.00 )=============================================


        Trion 'FreeSpace' Door.

        (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '94-'97. All rights reserved.

        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


   This is a little door that shows information about a volume.
   It shows the type, status, size, blocksize and free and
   used bytes.
   It also has a graph to show how full a volume is.


   You can use it as an indicator to the user of the Upload
   space that is available before the user starts his
   upload. So he can see if there is enough space.

   Here is an example of a simple upload command that
   uses this door:


Cmd "U"
   CliDoor  "doors:FreeSpace/FreeSpace DH1:"
   More
   Print "||Start Uploading now..||"
   Upload
EndCmd


   Also you can use it in a sysop menu, so you can check
   the status of drives:


Cmd "1"
   CliDoor  "doors:FreeSpace/FreeSpace DH1:"
   More
EndCmd

Cmd "2"
   CliDoor  "doors:FreeSpace/FreeSpace DH2:"
   More
EndCmd


   Use a -G flag if you only want the graph and not all the
   specifics of a volume.

   Note that you can use it for a removable media because the
   door won't cause a requester to popup if there is no
   media in the drive when this door in started.


